raw_response:
Looking at the bug, I need to understand what's happening in the loop that processes remaining tokens after the last creator property is found.

When the last creator property is assigned and the bean is built, the code enters a while loop to copy remaining FIELD_NAME tokens into the buffer. The issue is in this section:

```java
while (t == JsonToken.FIELD_NAME) {
    // NOTE: do NOT skip name as it needs to be copied; `copyCurrentStructure` does that
    p.nextToken(); /* bug is here */
    tokens.copyCurrentStructure(p);
    t = p.nextToken();
}
```

The comment says "do NOT skip name as it needs to be copied; `copyCurrentStructure` does that". But then `p.nextToken()` is called before `tokens.copyCurrentStructure(p)`, which skips the field name! The parser is advanced past the field name to the value, so `copyCurrentStructure` only copies the value, not the field name.

The fix is to NOT call `p.nextToken()` before `tokens.copyCurrentStructure(p)` - we should write the field name first and then copy the structure, or simply call `copyCurrentStructure` while the parser is still on the FIELD_NAME token so it copies both name and value.

Looking at the code, `copyCurrentStructure` when called on a FIELD_NAME token will copy the field name and its value. So we should NOT advance the parser before calling it:

