Looking at the bug, the issue is that when `locale` is `null`, the key used for cache lookup doesn't include the locale, so `format2` (created with `Locale.US` as default) and `format3` (created with `Locale.GERMANY` as default) end up with the same key and `format3` gets the cached `format2` (which has `Locale.US`).

The fix is to always include the locale in the key, resolving the default locale before constructing the key.

