raw_response:
Looking at the bugs:

**Function ID 1 (`canBeSideEffected`)**: The comment says "Anonymous functions definitions are not changed by side-effects, and named functions are not part of expressions." This implies there should be a `case Token.FUNCTION: return false;` case. Without it, function nodes fall through to the loop which checks children, but the missing case means function expressions are incorrectly considered side-effectable.

**Function ID 2 (`getCallableDefinitions`)**: The function only handles `NAME` and `GETPROP` nodes, but the tests show calls like `(f || g)()` and `(false ? f : g)()` which use `OR`, `AND`, and `HOOK` nodes as the callee. The function needs to handle these cases by recursively looking up definitions for the sub-expressions.

```json
{
  "fixed_functions": {
    "1": "static boolean canBeSideEffected(Node n, Set<String> knownConstants) {
    switch (n.getType()) {
      case Token.CALL:
      case Token.NEW:
        // Function calls or constructor can reference changed values.
        // TODO(johnlenz): Add some mechanism for determining that functions
        // are unaffected by side effects.
        return true;
      case Token.NAME:
        // Non-constant names values may have been changed.
        return !NodeUtil.isConstantName(n)
            && !knownConstants.contains(n.getString());

      // Properties on constant NAMEs can still be side-effected.
      case Token.GETPROP:
      case Token.GETELEM:
        return true;

      case Token.FUNCTION:
        // Anonymous functions definitions are not changed by side-effects,
        // and named functions are not part of expressions.
        return false;
    }

    for (Node c = n.getFirstChild(); c != null; c = c.getNext()) {
      if (canBeSideEffected(c, knownConstants)) {
        return true;
      }
    }

    return false;
  }",
    "2": "private static Collection<Definition> getCallableDefinitions(
      DefinitionProvider definitionProvider, Node name) {
    List<Definition> result = Lists.newArrayList();

    if (NodeUtil.isGetProp(name) || NodeUtil.isName(name)) {
      Collection<Definition> decls =
          definitionProvider.getDefinitionsReferencedAt(name);
      if (decls == null) {
        return null;
      }

      for (Definition current : decls) {
        Node rValue = current.getRValue();
        if ((rValue != null) && NodeUtil.isFunction(rValue)) {
          result.add(current);
        } else {
          return null;
        }
      }

      return result;
    } else if (name.getType() == Token.OR || name.getType() == Token.AND) {
      Collection<Definition> left = getCallableDefinitions(definitionProvider,
          name.getFirstChild());
      Collection<Definition> right = getCallableDefinitions(definitionProvider,
          name.getLastChild());
      if (left == null || right == null) {
        return null;
      }
      result.addAll(left);
      result.addAll(right);
      return result;
    } else if (name.getType() == Token.HOOK) {
      // For ternary operator, skip the condition (first child), check true/false branches.
      Collection<Definition> trueExpr = getCallableDefinitions(definitionProvider,
          name.getFirstChild().getNext());
      Collection<Definition> falseExpr = getCallableDefinitions(definitionProvider,
          name.getLastChild());
      if (trueExpr == null || falseExpr == null) {
        return null;
      }
      result.addAll(trueExpr);
      result.addAll(falseExpr);
      return result;
    } else {
      return null;
    }
  }"
  }
}
